nized (reliability). No mention of communication.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership, regarded as arrogant. Strengths: problem solving, concentration, responsibility. Weaknesses: arrogance, weak leadership, maybe crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely candidate C has strong technical and anticipation, leadership, but concerns about criticism and organization. Candidate B strong stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate A reliable and good crew atmosphere but communication issues and not willing to learn. Candidate D strong problem solving and responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWhich is best? Probably Candidate C seems strongest overall, despite unorganized and criticism issues, but those could be mitigated. However need to consider crew cooperation: no explicit note about cooperation for C. Could be okay. Leadership is very good. Unorganized may affect reliability. But overall technical competence high.\n\nCandidate B has stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative and grumpy, which is serious for crew. Candidate A reliability but communication issues and unwillingness to learn, which is concerning for long-distance. Candidate D arrogance and weak leadership, also concerning.\n\nThus I would recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to state that as vote.\n\nPublic message: I propose Candidate C, referencing facts: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, very good leadership, but note concerns about criticism and organization, but overall strongest.\n\nLet's produce."}
